        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "The probe is often pasted into an interactive shell, so the scaffold must never call exit at top level and its marker must not contain `!` (bash history expansion); the exit status therefore stays the clipboard tail's.",
            "coreutils timeout puts the bounded child in its own process group and signals the group (true of GNU coreutils, which the operator's WSL2 Ubuntu has); a busybox timeout that does not may leave a grandchild holding the capture until it exits."
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "Default bound 120 seconds, as the desk suggested.",
            "One bound over the whole body, not per command; -k 5 sends KILL five seconds after TERM, so the worst case is bound + 5 s.",
            "probe() runs in a child bash (`bash -c \"$(declare -f probe)\"`) in every path, bounded or not, so its semantics do not change with the variable; the scaffold comment tells the worker to keep everything inside probe().",
            "Once a bounded body finishes, its process group is killed, so a command left running in the background cannot hold the block open past the body.",
            "A cut is detected by timeout's 124/137 together with elapsed time >= the bound, so a body that merely exits 124 is not mislabelled.",
            "Marker wording: `*** PROBE CUT: probe() hit its N-second bound and was stopped; the lines above are partial. Rerun with BALE_PROBE_TIMEOUT=<seconds> for longer, or BALE_PROBE_TIMEOUT=0 for no bound. ***`; it joins the captured output so the unchanged trailer counts it.",
            "Exit status is not changed by a cut (no top-level exit; the clipboard tail's status stands); the cut is reported by the marker on stdout and a [probe] line on stderr.",
            "The bound line is a fifth purpose-header line, after the verbatim read-only line, so lines 1-4 keep their positions.",
            "gtimeout is accepted where timeout is absent (macOS with Homebrew coreutils); a timeout that rejects coreutils' arguments is reported and the body runs unbounded.",
            "An empty-but-set BALE_PROBE_TIMEOUT counts as a bad value (reported, default holds), not as unset.",
            "Reworded comment: `# Label column is capped: one pathological label must not drag every` / `# row's alignment out. ...` re-wrapped, rule unchanged.",
            "-B stays explicit beside -I because -I ignores PYTHON* variables, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE included.",
            "The changelog record lists the three surfaces the brief names, not docs/TARBALL.md, following 0.4.49's record, which left its doc change out of surfaces too."
          ],
